      "writtenOn": "2020-11-10T17:25:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, IIRC the whole story is that behind the hood of this lock is rcu_sync. when rcu_sync is in IDLE mode, it\u0027ll end-up with a synchronize_rcu(). As the access to this lock is serialized by the HP locks, cpu_write_lock() will always end-up in a synchronize_rcu().",
      "parentUuid": "effe57c4_9b12840e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1182,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 1182,
        "endChar": 23
