      "writtenOn": "2020-11-10T01:33:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you remind me why we need the cpus_write_lock() here?\nMy understanding is that cpus_read_lock() is used by various drivers to ensure the kernel isnt offlined while they work on it. \n\nsched_cpu_deactivate/activate isnt taking the cpu all the way to offline. So do we need cpus_write_lock()?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1187,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1187,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "cb20d3d39876d8bbd7f11c782ea6468807562100",
